From f802fcf9ea05abb232e7a6b5d3ce05363178a378 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tomas Glozar <tglozar@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 24 Aug 2026 21:25:27 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 523/634] IA64: mca: Bound the CPE poll cascade by nr_cpu_ids

ia64_mca_cpe_int_caller() checks the result of cpumask_next() against
NR_CPUS, but an exhausted cpumask_next() returns small_cpumask_bits,
which only equals NR_CPUS while NR_CPUS <= BITS_PER_LONG; above that it
is nr_cpu_ids. So on an 8-CPU machine built with NR_CPUS=128 the last
CPU of the cascade gets cpuid = 8, passes the NR_CPUS check and IPIs a
CPU that was never brought up.

cpu_physical_id() is -1 for such a CPU, and ia64_send_ipi() turns that
into a write to ipi_base_addr - 0x10, i.e. physical 0xfedffff0. Nothing
responds there, and on an rx2620 the zx1 reports the response timeout as
an uncorrected bus check during boot:

    Entered OS MCA handler. PSP=20010000fff21320 cpu=6 monarch=1

    Bus Error [00]
      Target ID          0x00000000fedffff0
    RT_ADDRa   0x9540    0x00340000fedffff0

psp.us is set, so the error is unrecoverable and the boot dies. This
only reproduces with NR_CPUS > 64.

Use nr_cpu_ids, as ia64_mca_cmc_int_caller() already does.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5
Signed-off-by: Tomas Glozar <tglozar@gmail.com>
---
 arch/ia64/kernel/mca.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/ia64/kernel/mca.c b/arch/ia64/kernel/mca.c
index 0598760e7b1e5..481325faaf9e0 100644
--- a/arch/ia64/kernel/mca.c
+++ b/arch/ia64/kernel/mca.c
@@ -1564,7 +1564,7 @@ ia64_mca_cpe_int_caller(int cpe_irq, void *arg)
 
 	cpuid = cpumask_next(cpuid+1, cpu_online_mask);
 
-	if (cpuid < NR_CPUS) {
+	if (cpuid < nr_cpu_ids) {
 		ia64_send_ipi(cpuid, IA64_CPEP_VECTOR, IA64_IPI_DM_INT, 0);
 	} else {
 		/*
